# Week 3 — Transfer Learning and Model Improvement

## Completed This Week

During Week 3, the baseline CNN model was improved using transfer learning and regularization techniques.

The following tasks were completed:

- Added data augmentation
- Implemented Dropout layers
- Used MobileNetV2 pretrained on ImageNet
- Trained an improved deep learning model
- Compared results with the Week 2 baseline CNN
- Generated updated accuracy plots

---

## Model Improvements

The original CNN model from Week 2 showed signs of overfitting.

To improve generalization performance, the following methods were added:

- Transfer Learning using MobileNetV2
- Data augmentation:
  - random flip
  - random rotation
  - random zoom
- Dropout regularization

The pretrained MobileNetV2 model was used as a feature extractor with frozen weights.

---

## Training Results

The improved model was trained for 5 epochs.

Final results:

| Metric | Result |
|---|---|
| Training Accuracy | ~85% |
| Validation Accuracy | ~88% |

The validation accuracy improved significantly compared to the Week 2 baseline model.

